<title>BELGIUM: U.S. wants EU to suspend grain export subsidies.</title>
<headline>U.S. wants EU to suspend grain export subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>ANTWERP, Belgium 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. has asked the European Union to consider dropping grain subsidies for the rest of 1996/97 (July/June), said George Pope, U.S. agricultural attache to the EU.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment we see no reason for continued subsidies on grain this marketing year,&quot; he told Reuters at the Lipidex '97 oilseeds conference.</p>
<p>&quot;The EU is the only player in the grain market for the next six weeks, so why subsidise?&quot;</p>
<p>Pope said the U.S. had repeatedly communicated this to the EU in writing and in direct talks.</p>
<p>But he conceded the EU was within its rights to subsidise under world trade regulations.</p>
<p>&quot;That's not in question. It's a marketing issue,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
